{
  "case_id": "2022-21-468",
  "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Pork Producers Council",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The facts we allege are assumed to be true for purposes of decision here. They state a claim that Proposition 12 violates the Commerce Clause almost per se because it's an extraterritorial regulation that conditions pork sales on out-of-state farmers adopting California's preferred farming methods, for no valid safety reason. Proposition 12 also fails the Pike test because it burdens interstate commerce for no local benefit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 21-468, National Pork Producers versus Ross."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I understand New York has a law that says that if you want to import firewood into the state, you have to have used a certain kind of pesticide to make sure that various pests don't come in with the firewood. Would that be forbidden?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I just clarify? Because I -- I perceive a difference in the rule that you're articulating right now than what's in your briefs, and I just want to make sure I understand the per se rule that you are articulating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Bishop, you have -- you have several arguments, and I gather that your answer to Justice Kagan based on your extraterritoriality argument is no, New York can't do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, why -- why isn't this Pike balancing test a bit reading too much into too little? It's one paragraph in a short unanimous opinion and it relies on three very old cases, Baldwin, Healy, and Brown, which were all --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would -- I think you touched on this in your final comments, but let me just make sure about it. Most of your argument seemed to be arguing the merits of the extraterritoriality argument and the Pike balancing argument to a lesser extent. But is that the question we have here? This is on the pleadings. So what is the standard that we're supposed to apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Bishop, suppose I asked you to for a moment ditch the extraterritoriality argument and just go to Pike balancing. What would your position sound like?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Bishop, just to follow up on Justice Kagan's line of questioning where we've kind of laid out the costs and benefits in our balancing test that you're asking us to do, why isn't that just a form of enshrining non-textual economic liberties in -- into the Constitution, something this Court --a project this Court disavowed a long time ago?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Counsel, I want to ask you about extraterritoriality. So can you tell me why you answered Justice Kagan that the labeling wouldn't matter? I mean, if it's a per se rule that you can't control what's going on in other states, and you said, well, it's just insignificant, it's de minimis, but wouldn't the per se rule, the principle, still apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. Let me just ask, because I don't --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Taking the allegations in the complaint as true, Proposition 12's sales ban is invalid under Pike because it imposes a substantial burden on interstate commerce without serving a legitimate local public interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California's disagreement with the manner in which pigs are housed in other states is not a cognizable local interest of California that could support the imposition of such a ban."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But, even under Pike balancing, how do we draw the line between those two scenarios based solely on whether the state is saying we don't like it because of what --of the way in which these animals were raised versus we don't like it because we think the animals are going to harm our people?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Again, I think it's the distinction between -- and it reflects the -- the horizontal federalism that --that is spread throughout the Constitution. California has to respect the autonomy of its sister states, the -- its sister state's ability to regulate conduct within its borders. And if Kentucky thinks that the -- a particular method of raising horses is okay, that's up to Kentucky. But the horizontal federalism and"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Does the United States have any position on whether regulating that is consistent with federal treaty law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Kneedler, if Petitioner did not claim that there were these unique tracing and separation problems, already could do the tracing, could do the separation, would you still say that there was a substantial burden on interstate commerce? And if so --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: I think it -- I think it's difficult to quantify, but let --let me make a -- an important antecedent point. Costs are a manifestation of the burdens on interstate commerce.\nBut, when California law requires a foreign producer to change its operation because California disagrees with the way it's done, that is itself a burden on interstate commerce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But here today the Petitioners kind of move away a little bit from the controlling effect idea, and they say the per se rule should be essentially focused on the nature of the regulation, that the state law that conditions sales on out-of-state businesses operating in a certain way is the principle. And that's the one that you seem to be agreeing with."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But isn't that the same thing he's saying when he says --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Mongan, does it matter whether or not you focus directly on the upstream effects, that that's the point of the legislation, as opposed to a collateral effect of your legislation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 111,
        "start": 111
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But how -- how -- how does the principle that you articulate relate to the concerns of the Dormant Commerce Clause? I mean, I had understood that part of the concern was that when states do the kind of thing that you're talking about, even if they are doing so to protect the products in --for a moral reason that are being sold into the state, it still has a significant impact on interstate commerce and that that's really what the Constitution cares about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0005-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 113,
        "start": 113
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: -- the problem that I'm having a little bit with --with your side of this case is that we're only at the motion to dismiss stage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus (Michigan and Illinois)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0005-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 118,
        "start": 118
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MONGAN: No, Your Honor, that's certainly not how I would put it. I think that this is a concern held by California and many other states, including states who are pork-producing, like Michigan and Illinois, who filed an amicus brief on our side, and it goes to core features of state sovereign authority to control the -- the products that are sold within our borders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 121,
        "start": 121
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, how broadly would you define \"immoral\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lamken",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0006-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 133,
        "start": 133
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Exxon makes clear that what the Commerce Clause prodects -- protects is interstate commerce, not particular methods of production or organization of industry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 134,
        "start": 134
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Are you giving up on the health and safety aspects of your claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0006-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "higher stocking density, so this is the intense confinement, correlates with higher salmonella rates for growing pigs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bishop",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdfb4f3491a102d5121840e3e1265f427098cb431b09ea5240d4ce2e6c7fb0a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdfb4f3491a-0006-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 144,
        "start": 144
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what I ask the Court to focus on is what our nation's interstate market looks like if California can condition sales on its moral or policy views and every other state can do the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-468",
